Here are my findings on the owner/member registration flow (Spring PetClinic REST). This is a read-only report; nothing was modified.

## 1. Classes involved in owner registration

- Controller: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java` (method `addOwner`, lines 129-172). A v2 controller also exists: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v2/OwnerRestControllerV2.java`.
- Service: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/ClinicServiceImpl.java` (interface `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/ClinicService.java`). Key methods: `saveOwner` (241-251), `countOwnersByRegistrationDate` (288-292).
- Entity: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java`.
- Repositories: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/OwnerRepository.java` plus JPA/JDBC/SpringData implementations under `.../repository/{jpa,jdbc,springdatajpa}/`.
- Supporting generators: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/CustomerCodeGenerator.java`, `.../service/HouseholdIdGenerator.java`.

## 2. Where registrationDate is set

It is NOT taken from the request. It is defaulted to the server date via a JPA `@PrePersist` callback on the entity.

`Owner.java:168-177`:
```java
@PrePersist
void defaultRegistrationDate() {
    if (this.registrationDate == null) {
        this.registrationDate = LocalDate.now();
    }
}
```
Field declaration `Owner.java:54-55`:
```java
@Column(name = "registration_date")
private LocalDate registrationDate;
```
Note: the default is a plain `LocalDate.now()` with NO weekend/business-day adjustment (see item 5 for the test that expects weekend roll-forward).

## 3. Membership number generation (year segment from registrationDate)

`Owner.java:138-144`:
```java
@Transient
public String getMembershipNumber() {
    if (this.customerCode == null || this.registrationDate == null) {
        return null;
    }
    return String.format("%s-M%02d", this.customerCode, this.registrationDate.getYear() % 100);
}
```
The "year segment" is `this.registrationDate.getYear() % 100` (last two digits of the registration year, zero-padded to 2 via `%02d`). The `customerCode` prefix is generated in `ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner` (lines 243-246) using `CustomerCodeGenerator`.

## 4. Daily create-limit enforcement (owners per day)

Enforced in the controller `addOwner`.

Constant `OwnerRestControllerV1.java:72`:
```java
private static final long MAX_OWNERS_PER_DAY = 100;
```
Check `OwnerRestControllerV1.java:148-150`:
```java
if (clinicService.countOwnersByRegistrationDate(LocalDate.now()) >= MAX_OWNERS_PER_DAY) {
    return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.TOO_MANY_REQUESTS);
}
```
This delegates to `ClinicServiceImpl.countOwnersByRegistrationDate` (`ClinicServiceImpl.java:288-292`) -> `OwnerRepository.countByRegistrationDate` (`OwnerRepository.java:112`), implemented as:
- SpringData JPA: `SpringDataOwnerRepository.java:72-73` (`SELECT COUNT(owner) FROM Owner owner WHERE owner.registrationDate = :registrationDate`)
- JPA: `JpaOwnerRepositoryImpl.java:157-160`
- JDBC: `JdbcOwnerRepositoryImpl.java:282-286` (`SELECT COUNT(*) FROM owners WHERE registration_date = :registrationDate`)

## 5. Existing related tests

- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java` — test `coreDefaultDateIsBusinessDay` (lines 14-19) asserts the default `registrationDate` is never Saturday/Sunday. The Javadoc (lines 9-11) states the intended invariant: "the default registration date must fall on a business day (a weekend rolls forward to Monday)."
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceBase.java` — contains the business-day/weekend/holiday helper `toBusinessDay` (lines 267-274) and the `HOLIDAYS` set (line 240), plus `sha256hex`/Luhn expectation helpers (from ~line 281).

Potential mismatch worth flagging: the test expects weekend roll-forward, but production code (`Owner.defaultRegistrationDate`, `Owner.java:172-177`) sets a raw `LocalDate.now()` with no weekend/holiday adjustment. On a weekend server date this invariant would not hold from the production side.

I found no dedicated tests specifically named for membership number or daily-limit beyond the above; the daily-limit path (`MAX_OWNERS_PER_DAY` / `TOO_MANY_REQUESTS`) has no matching test in `src/test`.

## 6. Date / business-day utility classes

- In production/main code: NONE. There is no business-day/date utility class anywhere under `src/main`. The only date logic is the inline `LocalDate.now()` in `Owner.defaultRegistrationDate` (Owner.java:172-177) and `PetAgeValidator` (`.../rest/validation/PetAgeValidator.java`, unrelated to registration).
- In test code only: the business-day helper lives in `AcceptanceBase.java` — `toBusinessDay(LocalDate)` (lines 267-274) with the `HOLIDAYS` set (line 240). There is no equivalent utility on the main side, so any weekend-handling logic the tests anticipate is currently not implemented in production.

Related non-registration date field for reference: `Visit.java:56` sets `this.date = LocalDate.now()` in its constructor.

